import{_ as a,o as t,c as n,a2 as r}from"./chunks/framework.oeh4wjV1.js";const f=JSON.parse('{"title":"Archenemy Commander","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"formats/archenemy/variants/commander.md","filePath":"formats/archenemy/variants/commander.md","lastUpdated":1792425987000}'),o={name:"formats/archenemy/variants/commander.md"};function s(i,e,h,l,d,c){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="archenemy-commander" tabindex="-1">Archenemy Commander <a class="header-anchor" href="#archenemy-commander" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Archenemy Commander&quot;">​</a></h1><p><a href="./../">Archenemy versions</a> · <strong>Rules: Commander team game</strong></p><h2 id="players-and-materials" tabindex="-1">Players and materials <a class="header-anchor" href="#players-and-materials" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Players and materials&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Choose one archenemy and a hero team, normally three or more heroes. Every player uses a legal Commander deck: 100 cards including the commander or commanders, the applicable color identity, and singleton construction except basic lands and explicit card exceptions.</p><p>The archenemy needs a scheme deck of <strong>at least ten cards with different English names</strong>. Prepare the tokens, counters, and commander-damage records required by the decks.</p><h2 id="setup" tabindex="-1">Setup <a class="header-anchor" href="#setup" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Setup&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Choose the archenemy and hero team.</li><li>Put each player&#39;s commander or commanders in their command zone. Shuffle ordinary libraries.</li><li>Shuffle the archenemy&#39;s scheme deck and keep it face down in the command zone.</li><li>The archenemy starts at <strong>60 life</strong>. The hero team starts with <strong>one shared total of 60 life</strong>, regardless of the number of heroes.</li><li>Each player draws seven and takes normal multiplayer mulligans.</li><li>The archenemy takes the first turn.</li></ol><p>Commander tax, commander-zone movement, and commander damage remain in effect.</p><h2 id="turns-and-combat" tabindex="-1">Turns and combat <a class="header-anchor" href="#turns-and-combat" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Turns and combat&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The archenemy takes the first turn and draws during their first draw step. Then the hero team takes a shared turn. Alternate archenemy turns and team turns.</p><p>During a team turn, heroes move through the phases and steps together. Each untaps their own permanents, takes their own draw, and may use their own land play. They make their own decisions, pay their own costs, and keep their own hands, libraries, mana, and permanents. Being teammates does not let them spend one another&#39;s mana or cards.</p><p>The heroes declare their attacks together against the archenemy or legal objects that can be attacked. When the archenemy attacks, declare which hero or attackable object each creature attacks. Heroes declare blockers together and can use their creatures to defend a teammate or that teammate&#39;s planeswalker. They cannot attack one another.</p><p>Use the shared-team-turn rules for priority, simultaneous decisions, and combat. Individual card restrictions still apply; being on a team does not allow an otherwise illegal target or block.</p><h2 id="shared-hero-life-and-individual-resources" tabindex="-1">Shared hero life and individual resources <a class="header-anchor" href="#shared-hero-life-and-individual-resources" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Shared hero life and individual resources&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Damage, life gain, and life loss affect the relevant player, then change the shared hero life total. A spell affecting each player or each opponent affects each hero separately; do not count the entire hero team as one target.</p><p>For example, if each of three heroes loses 2 life, their shared total falls by 6.</p><p>A cost or effect asking for a hero&#39;s life total uses the shared total. Paying life spends that shared resource; simultaneous life payments cannot exceed it. Setting one hero&#39;s life total adjusts the shared total accordingly. When an effect would set every hero&#39;s life, the team chooses one member to be affected. Teammates cannot exchange life totals with one another; redistribution can affect at most one member per team.</p><p>An effect preventing a hero from gaining life prevents the team&#39;s members from gaining life. An effect preventing a hero from losing life prevents team life loss and nonzero life payments. Apply the detailed shared-life rules in CR 810.9 for these interactions.</p><p>Poison counters are <strong>individual</strong>, with a threshold of <strong>ten</strong>, rather than the shared fifteen-poison rule from Two-Headed Giant. Record commander damage separately for each commander and each damaged player; do not pool damage from different commanders or different heroes.</p><h2 id="setting-schemes-in-motion" tabindex="-1">Setting schemes in motion <a class="header-anchor" href="#setting-schemes-in-motion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Setting schemes in motion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Keep the scheme deck shuffled, face down in the command zone, separate from the ordinary library. Its owner cannot inspect or rearrange it without an effect allowing that.</p><p>As the archenemy&#39;s precombat main phase begins on each of their turns, turn the top scheme face up in the command zone. This mandatory turn-based action sets the scheme in motion and does not use the stack. Abilities that trigger from it do use the stack, so players can respond to those abilities.</p><p>Choose targets when putting a triggered ability on the stack. Make choices or payments that the effect asks for during resolution at that time, rather than while revealing the scheme.</p><p>Schemes stay in the command zone. They are not battlefield permanents, cannot be cast, and cannot be destroyed with an effect that destroys a permanent. A face-up scheme&#39;s abilities function from the command zone.</p><h3 id="non-ongoing-schemes" tabindex="-1">Non-ongoing schemes <a class="header-anchor" href="#non-ongoing-schemes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Non-ongoing schemes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>A face-up, non-ongoing scheme goes face down on the bottom of its owner&#39;s scheme deck as a state-based action once no scheme triggered abilities are on the stack or waiting to be put there. Countering its ability does not leave the scheme permanently face up.</p><h3 id="ongoing-schemes" tabindex="-1">Ongoing schemes <a class="header-anchor" href="#ongoing-schemes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Ongoing schemes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>An ongoing scheme stays face up until an ability tells its controller to abandon it. Abandoning it turns it face down and puts it on the bottom of its owner&#39;s scheme deck. Its printed condition determines when that happens; revealing another scheme does not automatically abandon it.</p><p>Follow individual scheme instructions for additional schemes, costs, choices, and exceptions. A scheme asking an opponent to choose “self” or “others” still permits “others” when that opponent has no teammates, even if that option affects nobody.</p><h2 id="winning-and-losing" tabindex="-1">Winning and losing <a class="header-anchor" href="#winning-and-losing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Winning and losing&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Defeat the opposing side. This version uses the shared-life team win/loss rules referenced by CR 904.13b and 810.8: a team wins or loses together, including when one of its members wins or loses through an effect or another ordinary loss condition. A shared life total of zero or less causes the hero team to lose unless an applicable effect prevents it.</p><p>CR 904.13c specifically replaces shared poison with individual counters and the ten-counter threshold. Ordinary Commander damage remains a loss condition. Effects preventing a team member from winning or losing affect that team&#39;s result under the team rules. Conceding follows those team rules as well.</p><p>If both sides lose simultaneously, the game is a draw.</p><h2 id="other-versions-and-references" tabindex="-1">Other versions and references <a class="header-anchor" href="#other-versions-and-references" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Other versions and references&quot;">​</a></h2><p><a href="./standard.html">Standard Archenemy</a> uses separate hero life totals and a larger scheme deck. <a href="./rumble-commander.html">Commander Supervillain Rumble</a> gives every player schemes in a free-for-all.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://magic.wizards.com/en/formats/archenemy-commander" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wizards&#39; Archenemy Commander rules</a> and <a href="https://magic.wizards.com/en/rules" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Comprehensive Rules</a> 903, 904.13, 810.8, and 810.9.</p>',36)])])}const p=a(o,[["render",s]]);export{f as __pageData,p as default};
